    backToMethod: 'Read the AFR standard',
    botLink: 'What our own scanner fetches',
    ownerTitle: 'Owner mailbox (score-change notifications)',
    ownerBody:
      'A site owner can register one mailbox per domain and receive a mail when the AFR rating of that domain changes. Three locks guard it, and all three must open: (1) domain control — AFR hands out a challenge and reads it back from the domain itself (DNS TXT record, /.well-known/afr-mail.txt, or a homepage meta tag); (2) mailbox control — AFR mails a single-use confirmation link to that address; (3) the management token — that confirmation returns the token exactly once, and every later read or notification switch has to present it. The address is stored encrypted and is only ever reported masked (o***@example.com). The management token is never shown a second time: keep it (the AFR panel stores it in your own browser, nothing else does) — if you lose it, POST /api/v1/owners/email/recover hands out a new one: it re-proves domain control with a fresh challenge, mails the reset to the confirmed address only, and rotates the token so the old one stops working. Both write endpoints are gated by the same human check as the scans: the body carries "turnstile_token" (action afr_owner_email), a missing token is answered 400 { "error": "turnstile_failed" }, and the X-AFR-Agent-Key header skips the check for agents. Limits: 3 challenges and 3 registrations per domain per day, 5 per IP per hour.',
